# Line endings are LF in the repository, on every platform.
#
# Development happens on Windows and deployment is Debian, so without this the
# working tree gets CRLF from core.autocrlf while the committed blobs stay LF.
# Nothing breaks, but `gofmt -l` then reports every Go file as unformatted -
# the difference is the line endings and nothing else - which makes the check
# CLAUDE.md tells you to run useless, and `gofmt -w ./cmd ./internal` rewrites
# the whole tree and buries the change it was run alongside.
#
# The shell scripts and unit files are the load-bearing case rather than a
# tidiness one: they are executed on Debian, and CRLF in a shebang line is a
# "bad interpreter" error that names a file that plainly exists.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Real binaries, left alone.
*.db binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
